commands.doc:
Make a fraction of markups *arg1* and *arg2*.

```lilypond
\markup {
  π ≈ \fraction 355 113
}
```

Align *arg* in *axis* direction to the *dir* side.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \column {
    one
    \general-align #X #LEFT two
    three
    \null
    one
    \general-align #X #CENTER two
    three
    \null
    \line {
      one
      \general-align #Y #UP two
      three
    }
    \null
    \line {
      one
      \general-align #Y #3.2 two
      three
    }
  }
}
```

Draw horizontal brackets around *arg*.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \hbracket {
    \line {
      one two three
    }
  }
}
```

Center *arg* horizontally within a box of extending
*length*/2 to the left and right.

```lilypond
\new StaffGroup <<
  \new Staff {
    \set Staff.instrumentName = \markup {
      \hcenter-in #12 Oboe
    }
    c''1
  }
  \new Staff {
    \set Staff.instrumentName = \markup {
      \hcenter-in #12 Bassoon
    }
    \clef tenor
    c'1
  }
>>
```

Create an invisible object taking up *amount* horizontal space.

```lilypond
\markup {
  one
  \hspace #2
  two
  \hspace #8
  three
}
```

*amount* can be also a negative value, which can be best visualized as if
the current drawing point gets moved to the left.

```lilypond
\markup \concat {
  \hspace #4
  \column {
    \box \concat { AAAA \hspace #4 }
    \box \concat { AAAA \hspace #-4 }
    \box \concat { \hspace #4 AAAA }
    \box \concat { \hspace #-4 AAAA }
  }
}
```

See also `\abs-hspace`.

Justify the data that has been assigned to *symbol*.

```lilypond
\header {
  title = "My title"
  myText = "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur
    adipisicing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt
    ut labore et dolore magna aliqua.  Ut enim ad minim
    veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris
    nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat."
}

\paper {
  bookTitleMarkup = \markup {
    \column {
      \fill-line { \fromproperty #'header:title }
      \null
      \justify-field #'header:myText
    }
  }
}

\markup {
  \null
}
```

Align *arg* on its left edge.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \column {
    one
    \left-align two
    three
  }
}
```

Put *args* into a left-aligned column.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \left-column {
    one
    two
    three
  }
}
```

Put *args* into a horizontal line.

The property `word-space` determines the space between markups in
*args*.  For right-to-left scripts like Hebrew, `text-direction` should
be set to -1.

```lilypond
\markup
  \override #'(word-space . 3)
  \column {
    \line { "A B" "C D" "E F" }
    \override #'(text-direction . -1)
    \line { "A B" "C D" "E F" }
  }
```

Magnify current font by factor *sz* to print *arg*.

```lilypond
\markup {
  default
  \hspace #2
  \magnify #1.5 {
    50% larger
  }
}
```

Note that magnification only works if a font name is explicitly selected.  Use
`\fontsize` otherwise.

Draw a natural symbol.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \natural
}
```

Set *arg* in subscript with a normal font size.

```lilypond
\markup {
  default
  \normal-size-sub {
    subscript in standard size
  }
}
```

Set *arg* in superscript with a normal font size.

```lilypond
\markup {
  default
  \normal-size-super {
    superscript in standard size
  }
}
```

Print *arg* with default text font.

This resets all font-related properties (except the size), no matter what font
was used earlier.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \huge \bold \sans \fontCaps {
    huge bold sans caps
    \hspace #2
    \normal-text {
      huge normal
    }
    \hspace #2
    as before
  }
}
```

Switch to normal weight (in contrast to bold) to print *arg*.

This command sets the `font-series` property to `normal`.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \bold {
    some bold text
    \hspace #2
    \normal-weight {
      normal font series
    }
    \hspace #2
    bold again
  }
}
```

markup.doc:
Set font size to default (i.e., to value 0) to print *arg*.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \teeny {
    this is very small
    \hspace #2
    \normalsize {
      normal size
    }
    \hspace #2
    teeny again
  }
}
```

commands.doc:
An empty markup with extents of a single point.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \null
}
```

Take a list of markups *args* and combine them.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \fontsize #5
  \override #'(thickness . 2)
  \overlay {
    \draw-line #'(0 . 4)
    \arrow-head #Y #DOWN ##f
    \translate #'(0 . 4) \arrow-head #Y #UP ##f
  }
}
```

Add padding *amount* all around *arg*.

Identical to function `\pad-markup`.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \box {
    default
  }
  \hspace #2
  \box {
    \pad-around #0.5 {
      padded
    }
  }
}
```

Add padding *amount* all around *arg*.

Identical to function `\pad-around`.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \box {
    default
  }
  \hspace #2
  \box {
    \pad-markup #1 {
      padded
    }
  }
}
```

Make *arg* take at least *x-ext*, *y-ext* space.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \box {
    default
  }
  \hspace #4
  \box {
    \pad-to-box #'(0 . 10) #'(0 . 3) {
      padded
    }
  }
}
```

Add padding *amount* around *arg* in the X direction.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \box {
    default
  }
  \hspace #4
  \box {
    \pad-x #2 {
      padded
    }
  }
}
```

Add padding *amount* to the left of *arg* in the X direction.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \box {
    default
  }
  \hspace #4
  \box {
    \pad-x-left #2 {
      padded
    }
  }
}
```

Add padding *amount* to the right of *arg* in the X direction.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \box {
    default
  }
  \hspace #4
  \box {
    \pad-x-right #2 {
      padded
    }
  }
}
```

Add a link to a score's page *page-number* around *arg*.

This only works in the PDF backend.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \page-link #2 { \italic { This links to page 2... } }
}
```

markup.doc:
Draw parentheses around *arg*.

This is useful for parenthesizing a column containing several lines of text.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \parenthesize
  \column {
    foo
    bar
  }
  \override #'(angularity . 2)
  \parenthesize
  \column {
    bah
    baz
  }
}
```

commands.doc:
Prepend *more* to all markup in *arg* tagged with *tag*.

It works similar to `\pushToTag` for music,
but only with markups.

```lilypond
tagged = \markup {
  \tag #'foo A
  \tag #'bar B
}

\markup { \push-to-tag #'foo prefoo \tagged }
```

Add *more* to the front of *music* tagged with *tag*.

A post-event can be added to the articulations of rhythmic events or chords;
other expressions may be added to chords, sequential or simultaneous music.

Remove markup from *arg* that is tagged with *tags*.

The removed markup is replaced with empty stencils.
It works similar to `\removeWithTag` for music,
but only with markups.

```lilypond
tagged = \markup {
  \tag #'foo A
  \tag #'bar B
}

\markup { \remove-with-tag #'foo \tagged }
\markup { \remove-with-tag #'bar \tagged }
```

Draw embedded rhythmic pattern as specified by *music*.

```lilypond
\relative {
  \tempo \markup {
    Swing
    \hspace #0.4
    \rhythm { 8[ 8] } = \rhythm { \tuplet 3/2 { 4 8 } }
  }
  b8 g' c, d ees d16 ees d c r8
}
```

Within `\rhythm`, there is no time signature and no division in measures
(as with `\cadenzaOn`, Unmetered music).  Beaming must
be added explicitly with the syntax explained in Manual beams.

```lilypond
\markup {
  The rhythmic pattern \rhythm { 16[ 8 16] } is
  a type of syncopation.
}
```

`\stemDown` can be used to flip the stems.

```lilypond
\markup \rhythm { \stemDown 8 16 8 }
```

`\rhythm` works by creating a `StandaloneRhythmVoice` context,
which is enclosed in a `StandaloneRhythmStaff` context, which is
enclosed in a `StandaloneRhythmScore` context. It is possible to
apply global tweaks to the output by using a `\layout` block.

```lilypond
\layout {
  \context {
    \StandaloneRhythmVoice
    \xNotesOn
  }
}

\markup \rhythm { 8 16 8 }
```

Align *arg* on its right edge.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \column {
    one
    \right-align two
    three
  }
}
```

Put *args* into a right-aligned column.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \right-column {
    one
    two
    three
  }
}
```

Rotate *arg* by *ang* degrees around its center.

```lilypond
\markup {
  default
  \hspace #2
  \rotate #45
  \line {
    rotated 45°
  }
}
```

Draw a box with rounded corners around *arg*.

This function looks at properties `thickness`, `box-padding`, and
`font-size` to determine the line thickness and padding around the
*arg*.  The `corner-radius` property defines the radius of the round
corners (default value is 1).

```lilypond
c4^\markup {
  \rounded-box {
    Overtura
  }
}
c,8. c16 c4 r
```

Note that the box does not horizontally displace its argument.  Use markup
commands like `\left-align` or `\table` to make LilyPond realign
it.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \override #'(box-padding . 1.5)
  \column {
    "text"
    \rounded-box "text"
    \left-align \rounded-box "text"
  }
}
```

Print *arg* with a sans-serif font.

This command sets the `font-family` property to `sans`.

```lilypond
\markup {
  default
  \hspace #2
  \sans {
    sans serif
  }
}
```

Scale *arg*.

*factor-pair* is a pair of numbers representing the scaling factor of the X
and Y axes.  Negative values may be used to produce mirror images.

```lilypond
\markup {
  \line {
    \scale #'(2 . 1)
    stretched
    \scale #'(1 . -1)
    mirrored
  }
}
```

markup.doc:
Scores within markup
Inline an image of music as specified by *score*.

The reference point (usually the middle staff line) of the lowest staff in the
top system is placed on the baseline.

No page breaks and no MIDI output, i.e., both `\pageBreak` commands and
`\midi{}` blocks get ignored.

```lilypond
\markup {
  Text before the score.
  \score {
    \new PianoStaff <<
      \new Staff \relative c' {
        \key f \major
        \time 3/4
        \mark \markup { Allegro }
        f2\p( a4)
      }
      \new Staff \relative c {
        \clef bass
        \key f \major
        \time 3/4
        f8( a c a c a
      }
    >>

    \layout {
      indent = 0.0\cm
    }
  }
  Text after the score.
}
```

